From 85989c007d6e1ba13ceff3c9d179815ea7b3900c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ant=C3=B3nio=20Sarmento?= <Keyaku@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 00:29:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] TcpInfo: skip a short tcp_info instead of desynchronising the
 caller

TcpInfo's constructor rejects a tcp_info shorter than it needs and throws before
reaching the line that advances the buffer past the attribute. parse() catches
that and returns null, but the position is still inside the tcp_info payload, so
TcpSocketTracker.parseSockInfo() reads the next rtattr header out of that payload
-- garbage lengths, then a BufferUnderflowException, then a Log.wtf carrying the
whole ~60 KB buffer as base64 into dropbox. On this device that is every socket
on every poll: one WTF every ~20 seconds, indefinitely.

The trigger is the kernel. tcpi_segs_in and tcpi_segs_out were added in Linux
4.2; this port runs 3.18, whose struct tcp_info ends at tcpi_max_pacing_rate, so
the length guard can never pass. Nothing turns the feature off either --
Dependencies.isTcpInfoParsingSupported() is a bare API-level test.

Advance the buffer in a finally so a short tcp_info is skipped cleanly. The
success path is unchanged: the constructor already leaves the position there.
tcpInfo stays null on this kernel, which is unavoidable, but INET_DIAG_MARK and
the socket accounting keep working and the attribute loop stays in step.

XDPLUS-DROP-WHEN: kernel >= 4.2, where tcpi_segs_in exists and the guard passes,
making this patch inert. Also drop it if AOSP fixes this upstream -- as of
2026-09-14 platform/packages/modules/NetworkStack main still throws before
advancing, with no finally, so there is nothing to cherry-pick.

Changes:
- Advance past the attribute in `TcpInfo.parse()` whether or not the constructor threw

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I1d872a238f304c8784321ecc2ce03da530a9fa82
---
 src/com/android/networkstack/netlink/TcpInfo.java | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/com/android/networkstack/netlink/TcpInfo.java b/src/com/android/networkstack/netlink/TcpInfo.java
index 31a408f..924c44e 100644
--- a/src/com/android/networkstack/netlink/TcpInfo.java
+++ b/src/com/android/networkstack/netlink/TcpInfo.java
@@ -139,12 +139,17 @@ public class TcpInfo {
     /** Parse a TcpInfo from a giving ByteBuffer with a specific length. */
     @Nullable
     public static TcpInfo parse(@NonNull ByteBuffer bytes, int infolen) {
+        final int start = bytes.position();
         try {
             return new TcpInfo(bytes, infolen);
         } catch (BufferUnderflowException | BufferOverflowException | IllegalArgumentException
                 | IndexOutOfBoundsException e) {
             Log.e(TAG, "parsing error.", e);
             return null;
+        } finally {
+            // The constructor can throw before it skips the attribute, which would leave
+            // the caller's attribute loop reading the next header out of this payload.
+            bytes.position(Math.min(infolen + start, bytes.limit()));
         }
     }
 
